WEBVTT

00:03.440 --> 00:05.810
Mother, please tell me...

00:06.360 --> 00:11.280
Is it true that my starry-eyed knight is actually not Francis, the White Rose, but...

00:11.740 --> 00:13.780
...the Black Rose instead?

00:14.660 --> 00:17.160
Who is the one I fell in love with?

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
NAAJA

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
Nadja,

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
With your eyes

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
Nadja,

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
NAAJA

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
What do you see?

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
Nani ga mieru

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
The door to the future,

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
Mirai no tobira

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
Sagashite iru

00:43.560 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
Minna egao de aetara

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
It could be so much more fun

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
I will go waving

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
Te wo furinagara

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
But I won't look back

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
Nadja, Your smile

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Under the blue sky,

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Aoi sora no shita de

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
I will find the place

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
Ashita no yukue

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
where my future lies

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
Mitsukeru kara

01:55.990 --> 01:58.030
﻿I just don't know...

02:00.530 --> 02:02.660
﻿I wonder... if you'd take that.

02:04.080 --> 02:05.870
﻿For... my mother.

02:25.390 --> 02:27.060
﻿My starry... eyed... knight!

02:27.930 --> 02:29.020
﻿I told you, didn't I?

02:29.440 --> 02:31.900
﻿You must never part with this brooch.

02:33.270 --> 02:35.480
﻿There are two... Francis's

02:36.690 --> 02:37.900
﻿The Black Rose!

02:38.650 --> 02:41.860
﻿I like all of you even more than before.

02:43.870 --> 02:45.950
﻿Which one is the one I like?

02:44.470 --> 02:45.310
Nadja!

02:45.950 --> 02:46.950
﻿Nadja!!

02:47.080 --> 02:49.160
﻿Hey, Nadja!!

02:49.410 --> 02:50.370
﻿Rita.

02:50.460 --> 02:51.420
﻿It's all black!

02:52.420 --> 02:53.960
﻿The pot is burning!

02:54.420 --> 02:55.130
﻿Oh, no!

02:55.420 --> 02:56.710
﻿Rita, hold this!

03:09.160 --> 03:14.130
The High-Flying Kennosuke!

03:14.770 --> 03:16.520
﻿What the heck happened?! Look at this!

03:16.860 --> 03:19.360
﻿You were in charge of making lunch today!

03:20.240 --> 03:21.950
I'm ﻿sorry. I'll make it again right away.

03:22.660 --> 03:24.570
﻿Wow, how beautiful!

03:24.570 --> 03:27.580
﻿please be careful not to break that.

03:28.080 --> 03:30.080
﻿That's because it's very precious to me.

03:30.500 --> 03:31.660
﻿It's okay.

03:32.210 --> 03:36.090
﻿After all, Nadja got this kaleidoscope from someone she likes, right?

03:36.460 --> 03:37.670
﻿Oh, Rita!

03:38.300 --> 03:38.800
﻿Geez!

03:38.800 --> 03:40.720
If you have time to look at that thing...

03:41.090 --> 03:43.180
﻿Why don't you practice your flamenco?

03:43.470 --> 03:47.100
Didn't you say you were going to perfect your flamenco?

03:47.100 --> 03:47.970
﻿What?!

03:47.970 --> 03:51.730
﻿Well, all you ever do is the same "lainuki".

03:51.730 --> 03:52.940
What did you say?!

03:58.020 --> 03:59.780
﻿Don't make fun of the samurai!

03:59.990 --> 04:01.690
﻿You dummy!

04:01.990 --> 04:03.070
Dummy?!

04:03.450 --> 04:05.950
﻿Well, you re a bowlegged rocks-for-brains!

04:05.950 --> 04:06.820
﻿What?!

04:06.830 --> 04:08.780
﻿Well, you're as skinny as a skeleton and as ugly as an old woman!

04:11.080 --> 04:13.000
﻿STOP!

04:13.420 --> 04:15.670
﻿No fighting! Right?

04:25.260 --> 04:28.260
﻿Nadja, Kennosuke, that's enough.

04:28.640 --> 04:32.270
﻿You'll spoil this meal if you eat with faces like that.

04:36.610 --> 04:37.350
﻿May I be excused?

04:38.940 --> 04:40.780
﻿You left your soup.

04:42.940 --> 04:45.400
﻿I can't drink that slop you call soup!

04:45.610 --> 04:46.740
﻿What did you say?!

04:47.870 --> 04:49.410
﻿I made it all over again!

04:53.370 --> 04:55.120
﻿What's with that attitude?!

04:55.290 --> 04:56.870
﻿Wait up!

04:59.540 --> 05:01.500
﻿If you want to fight, do it after the meal!

05:01.820 --> 05:02.240
Yes...

05:05.470 --> 05:06.220
﻿It's good!

05:10.430 --> 05:12.060
﻿Master, are you sure it's okay?

05:12.060 --> 05:14.060
﻿Leaving those two like that?

05:16.230 --> 05:17.310
﻿Let them do what they want.

05:19.900 --> 05:21.980
Kennosuke's getting way too angry here!

05:22.190 --> 05:23.280
﻿Well, hmph to him!

05:23.280 --> 05:25.950
﻿Kennosuke just didn't like it very much.

05:25.950 --> 05:27.660
﻿Huh? What?

05:28.660 --> 05:29.410
﻿Why?

05:31.410 --> 05:34.660
﻿You should be mature and apologize, Nadja.

05:36.500 --> 05:38.790
Nadja's a big idiot!

05:39.040 --> 05:39.920
﻿She's such a moron!

05:41.840 --> 05:43.670
﻿That kaleidoscope was just probably...

05:43.710 --> 05:46.970
﻿a present from some certain stuck-up guy.

05:47.970 --> 05:49.840
﻿Ahh! I hate this!

05:50.010 --> 05:51.720
﻿I understand how you feel, but...

05:52.180 --> 05:53.970
﻿Don't be stubborn.

05:54.100 --> 05:55.770
﻿Just make up with her.

05:56.140 --> 05:58.020
﻿Nadja's the one who's at fault.

05:58.140 --> 05:59.900
﻿All she does is look at that kaleidoscope.

05:59.900 --> 06:01.270
﻿Well, yes, but

06:01.730 --> 06:03.610
﻿Kennosuke, you're such a child.

06:04.190 --> 06:05.440
Wh-What...?

06:05.530 --> 06:09.740
﻿A girl is happy with any present from a guy she likes.

06:09.740 --> 06:10.910
﻿Right?

06:11.490 --> 06:12.910
If you ﻿can't understand that...

06:13.450 --> 06:15.490
﻿It's proof that... you're still a child.

06:16.000 --> 06:18.250
﻿I don't want to hear that from a real child!

06:19.500 --> 06:22.960
﻿Kennosuke. I know you want to make up with her.

06:23.300 --> 06:25.840
﻿Yeah. I may have said a little too much...

06:25.840 --> 06:27.510
﻿Then, apologize.

06:27.920 --> 06:30.300
﻿That's the kindness of a real man.

06:30.470 --> 06:31.470
That is.

06:31.720 --> 06:34.850
﻿Be a man and apologize to her.

06:37.390 --> 06:41.440
﻿...Mucho la-la-la-la, la-la, la-la...

06:41.440 --> 06:44.360
﻿...Mucho la-la-la-la la-la la..

06:45.530 --> 06:46.570
﻿Kennosuke...

06:48.150 --> 06:51.780
﻿You should be mature and apologize, Nadja.

06:52.870 --> 06:56.330
﻿Be a man and apologize to her.

06:57.500 --> 06:58.790
﻿Hey!
Hey...

06:59.410 --> 07:00.460
﻿G-Go ahead.

07:00.580 --> 07:02.290
﻿W-Why don't you go first, Kennosuke?

07:03.000 --> 07:04.380
﻿I can wait.

07:04.790 --> 07:06.050
﻿So, what is it?

07:06.380 --> 07:08.130
I can wait, too.

07:08.590 --> 07:11.130
﻿You have something you want to say to me, don't you Kennosuke?

07:12.340 --> 07:14.800
﻿I said it can wait!

07:15.930 --> 07:18.560
﻿Why don't you be a man and just say it?

07:18.560 --> 07:20.480
﻿Being a man or woman has nothing to do with this!

07:20.480 --> 07:23.020
﻿If you have something to say, then why don't you say it?!

07:23.230 --> 07:24.650
﻿Quit being so bossy!

07:24.650 --> 07:25.860
﻿What?!

07:30.450 --> 07:32.400
﻿If you're not going to talk, then stop interrupting me!

07:32.740 --> 07:34.200
﻿Whatever! Do what you want!

07:34.450 --> 07:35.570
﻿I will!

07:40.620 --> 07:45.670
﻿A, P, L, E... Apple!

07:46.590 --> 07:49.340
﻿Almost! You need one more "P".

07:51.050 --> 07:54.130
﻿Apple is AP-PLE.

07:55.010 --> 07:58.850
﻿See, it's A, P, P, L, E.

07:59.020 --> 08:00.640
﻿Oh, I see.

08:03.140 --> 08:04.730
﻿Where's Kennosuke?

08:04.940 --> 08:06.400
﻿Kennosuke!

08:06.400 --> 08:07.190
﻿I'm over here!

08:08.190 --> 08:12.740
﻿I 'm going to sec Mrs. Ramilez in Monte Frio. I need you to come with me.

08:13.950 --> 08:16.950
﻿It's my day off and I want to rest. I'm going to pass on it.

08:16.950 --> 08:17.910
﻿No you're not!

08:18.120 --> 08:19.580
﻿Why?!

08:19.580 --> 08:20.910
﻿I'm ordering you to.

08:21.330 --> 08:24.120
﻿If you don't come, you're fired from the Dandelion Troupe.

08:24.330 --> 08:25.710
﻿What?!

08:26.130 --> 08:28.840
﻿He ordered me... what a tyrant.

08:30.880 --> 08:32.420
﻿You're with us, too, Nadja?

08:33.340 --> 08:34.220
﻿What about it?

08:34.300 --> 08:36.140
﻿Excuse me for being with you.

08:36.340 --> 08:37.590
﻿Where are you going?

08:38.010 --> 08:39.560
﻿What do you care?

08:42.140 --> 08:42.930
﻿Kennosuke!

08:43.180 --> 08:43.770
﻿Hey!

08:44.810 --> 08:46.480
﻿Stop being stubborn, and come down!

08:48.860 --> 08:51.030
﻿If you stay in the sun like that...

08:51.030 --> 08:52.360
﻿You'll get sunburned!

08:53.570 --> 08:54.700
﻿I can take it!

09:06.540 --> 09:08.000
﻿It's hot...

09:09.420 --> 09:13.420
﻿Kennosuke, you'll die from sun stroke. Come down.

09:14.970 --> 09:17.470
﻿Die...? Maybe, I should get down...

09:17.840 --> 09:19.390
﻿Granny, you're insulting him.

09:19.640 --> 09:21.850
A ﻿samurai has more guts!

09:22.470 --> 09:27.600
﻿He wouldn't come down just because of hearing he'll die from sun stroke.

09:28.150 --> 09:30.980
﻿"A samurai never dies!" Right~?

09:31.570 --> 09:33.980
﻿NADJA!!!

09:33.990 --> 09:36.030
﻿Geez. Those two idiots.

09:36.070 --> 09:37.740
﻿Oh, George?

09:38.530 --> 09:44.080
﻿We still have time. Why don't we stop at that place before we go to Monte Frio?

09:44.500 --> 09:47.000
﻿Ah! I was just thinking the same thing.

09:47.830 --> 09:51.250
﻿Maybe these idiots will straighten up after they see that.

09:57.680 --> 10:00.800
﻿It's so hot. I'm starting to see things.

10:01.180 --> 10:03.390
﻿Everything is turning yellow...

10:10.520 --> 10:12.650
﻿Wow!! This is great!

10:13.110 --> 10:13.980
﻿Kennosuke!

10:14.320 --> 10:16.030
﻿What are you yelling about?

10:16.610 --> 10:19.110
﻿Nadja! Come out! It's amazing!

10:21.280 --> 10:23.780
﻿Looks like we're here.

10:25.790 --> 10:27.660
﻿What's the matter, Kennosuke?

10:27.660 --> 10:29.540
﻿Nadja, look out front.

10:32.420 --> 10:34.130
﻿Wh-What is this?!

10:34.750 --> 10:35.250
﻿Sunflowers?

10:36.090 --> 10:38.920
﻿Sunflowers! Sunflowers!!

10:41.090 --> 10:42.470
﻿It's wonderful! Wonderful!

10:42.850 --> 10:45.720
﻿Wonderful, wonderful, wonderful! Wonderful!!!

10:46.310 --> 10:49.310
﻿For Granny and I, this is our favorite place in Spain.

10:49.520 --> 10:53.810
﻿Anybody would fall in love with this view at first sight!

10:53.820 --> 10:54.730
﻿Right, Nadja?

10:54.730 --> 10:55.320
﻿Yeah!

10:55.780 --> 10:57.900
﻿I feel as if my heart is going to explode!

11:02.510 --> 11:03.390
Me, too!

11:07.870 --> 11:10.120
﻿Looks like it was worth it to bring them here.

11:11.330 --> 11:12.250
﻿Yeah.

11:43.070 --> 11:44.070
﻿Lo~!

11:44.600 --> 11:45.220
"Lo"?

11:49.100 --> 11:52.230
Paris is sunnier than London

11:52.230 --> 11:55.360
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

11:55.900 --> 12:02.030
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

12:03.160 --> 12:04.030
Indeed

12:03.800 --> 12:06.180
﻿That's the way she originally used to dance, wasn't it?

12:07.080 --> 12:09.540
It's no use worrying about it

12:09.540 --> 12:13.120
Que sera sera, sera sera

12:13.460 --> 12:18.000
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

12:18.210 --> 12:19.550
To be, to be

12:19.760 --> 12:24.760
The tree frog won

12:25.340 --> 12:29.850
the world frog-jumping contest

12:27.740 --> 12:29.490
I ﻿made myself dizzy...!

12:30.620 --> 12:31.580
﻿Nadja!

12:31.580 --> 12:32.660
﻿I'm okay.

12:32.640 --> 12:38.820
Under the kitten's paw

12:37.000 --> 12:38.290
﻿Sunflowers... huh?

12:39.020 --> 12:45.660
is the scent of the sun, right?

12:47.680 --> 12:48.510
﻿Kennosuke!

12:49.890 --> 12:51.810
I love sunflowers.

12:52.350 --> 12:55.390
﻿It lives with all it's might, facing the sun.

12:58.940 --> 13:00.690
﻿Kennosuke, what's the matter...

13:01.820 --> 13:03.740
﻿Oh, it's nothing.

13:05.320 --> 13:06.150
﻿Now that I think about it...

13:06.990 --> 13:09.910
﻿that person was like a sunflower, too...

13:14.120 --> 13:17.170
﻿At that time, we had been orphaned...

13:17.170 --> 13:19.750
﻿And, after having been passed around amongst our relatives,

13:19.750 --> 13:21.500
I ﻿was separated from my little sister..

13:21.550 --> 13:23.280
﻿Brother!

13:22.050 --> 13:25.470
﻿I was sent to a carpenter to be an apprentice.

13:23.610 --> 13:25.470
Hanako!

13:25.470 --> 13:27.470
﻿Brother!

13:27.640 --> 13:28.640
﻿Hanako...

13:30.850 --> 13:32.430
﻿If you keep crying like that...

13:32.930 --> 13:34.730
﻿the sunflowers will laugh at you.

13:36.140 --> 13:37.600
﻿I'm not crying...!

13:40.650 --> 13:43.190
﻿Hey! I am not crying!

13:43.190 --> 13:45.610
﻿Yes! That's the spirit, kid

13:46.200 --> 13:47.530
I'm ﻿not a kid!

13:47.660 --> 13:49.990
﻿I'm Tsurugi Kennosuke!

13:51.830 --> 13:52.830
﻿Well, please excuse my rudeness.

13:53.540 --> 13:55.790
﻿Kennosuke, would you like to fly this with me?

13:56.460 --> 13:57.870
﻿What's that?

13:58.080 --> 13:59.750
﻿It's an aeroplane that I made.

14:00.340 --> 14:01.590
﻿Aeroplane?

14:01.840 --> 14:04.710
﻿You rifle in it to fly in the sky like a bird.

14:09.470 --> 14:11.300
﻿It-it flew, uncle!

14:11.300 --> 14:12.800
﻿I'm hurt that you call me uncle.

14:13.260 --> 14:14.970
I'm Ninomiya Chuuhachi.

14:15.060 --> 14:16.980
﻿You can call me Chuu-san.

14:18.270 --> 14:19.640
Chuu-san, you're amazing.

14:19.980 --> 14:23.020
﻿My dream is to build an aeroplane that people can ride in.

14:23.150 --> 14:25.650
﻿Wow! Is that possible?

14:25.900 --> 14:27.150
﻿Of course!

14:27.450 --> 14:29.820
﻿If you try hard enough, you'll always catch your dream.

14:32.870 --> 14:33.870
﻿Uh! This is bad!

14:35.410 --> 14:36.700
﻿Chuu-san!

14:40.920 --> 14:41.580
﻿Your dream...

14:42.130 --> 14:44.250
﻿You'll always catch your dream!

14:46.170 --> 14:47.260
﻿I know it...

14:49.010 --> 14:50.430
﻿I'm sure of it..

14:54.760 --> 14:56.520
﻿A long time ago, I was poor...

14:56.520 --> 14:58.680
﻿and because I didn't have any money I didn't get an education.

14:59.060 --> 14:59.770
﻿But, you know...

15:00.140 --> 15:02.900
﻿I had a. mountain of things\ I wanted to do and learn.

15:03.190 --> 15:05.320
﻿So, I worked as hard as I could.

15:05.360 --> 15:06.780
﻿And, with the money that I earned..

15:07.240 --> 15:09.320
﻿I bought books to fulfill my dreams...

15:09.650 --> 15:12.320
﻿and learned things from many different teachers.

15:13.370 --> 15:15.120
﻿You're amazing, Chuu-san.

15:15.620 --> 15:17.080
﻿I'm not amazing.

15:17.580 --> 15:20.620
﻿If you have a dream, it gives you a reason to work hard.

15:22.460 --> 15:24.920
﻿I know! Why don't you come to my house?

15:25.710 --> 15:26.550
﻿I want to show you...

15:26.710 --> 15:29.010
﻿an aeroplane that people can ride in.

15:29.010 --> 15:30.170
Yes! I'll come!

15:35.180 --> 15:36.850
﻿If you attach an engine this will fly.

15:37.430 --> 15:41.230
﻿But, in order to carry people, it will have to be 5 to 6 times larger.

15:41.730 --> 15:45.230
﻿It's amazing, Chuu-san! It's a world-shaking invention!

15:45.440 --> 15:46.520
﻿Maybe.

15:46.820 --> 15:49.900
﻿I made that while I was working for the military.

15:50.240 --> 15:53.110
﻿But, to make a real one, a single person's wealth isn't good enough.

15:53.490 --> 15:56.530
﻿I applied many times to the military higher-ups, but...

15:56.700 --> 15:57.580
﻿They said no?

15:58.580 --> 16:01.250
﻿They said it was too fantastic, and refused.

16:01.660 --> 16:04.330
﻿That's why I'm trying to save enough money on my own...

16:04.630 --> 16:06.880
﻿by working a regular job at a company.

16:07.880 --> 16:13.510
﻿Since then... since then, I went to see him on my days off...

16:13.840 --> 16:15.760
﻿He would tell me so many stories...

16:16.140 --> 16:18.010
﻿or, we'd build model aeroplanes together...

16:18.100 --> 16:19.810
﻿and fly them.

16:21.230 --> 16:26.940
﻿I believed that Chuu-san would build the first passenger aeroplane in the world.

16:27.610 --> 16:28.480
﻿But...

16:28.480 --> 16:29.900
﻿But?

16:30.320 --> 16:32.690
﻿The first people to fly an aeroplane in the world were...

16:32.740 --> 16:34.450
﻿the Wright brothers of America.

16:35.820 --> 16:36.700
﻿He cried.

16:40.620 --> 16:42.700
﻿They did it before he could.

16:45.080 --> 16:47.000
﻿Chuu-san cried for a long time.

16:49.050 --> 16:52.380
﻿But, in the end, he smiled.

16:53.630 --> 16:57.470
﻿I'm going to give up on aeroplanes, and find another dream.

16:58.260 --> 16:59.890
H﻿aving a dream is a good thing.

17:00.180 --> 17:02.100
﻿The bigger the better.

17:02.850 --> 17:04.140
﻿So, Kennosuke...

17:05.100 --> 17:06.940
﻿Keep going towards your dream!

17:07.980 --> 17:09.980
﻿Don't stay in this small country of Japan.

17:09.980 --> 17:11.820
﻿Get out into the wide world.

17:12.070 --> 17:15.280
﻿And, gather the knowledge necessary for your dream.

17:21.290 --> 17:22.200
﻿Chuu-san...

17:24.080 --> 17:25.460
﻿That's a sad story.

17:26.170 --> 17:28.210
﻿But, Chuu-san gave me...

17:29.380 --> 17:31.290
﻿The courage to live my life!

17:31.920 --> 17:34.630
﻿I jumped on a ship heading towards France.

17:34.970 --> 17:37.880
﻿For my dream... in order to realize my dream!

17:42.430 --> 17:45.100
﻿What is your dream, Kennosuke?

17:45.560 --> 17:46.690
﻿My dream is...

17:47.140 --> 17:49.350
﻿...to master mechanics. And, someday...

17:49.810 --> 17:52.520
﻿...create a machine that can fly people to the moon!

17:54.400 --> 17:55.490
﻿That's wonderful.

17:55.490 --> 17:56.740
﻿I think that's great.

17:58.780 --> 18:00.660
﻿You can do it, Kennosuke.

18:01.280 --> 18:02.450
﻿Thank you...

18:05.180 --> 18:06.060
I...

18:09.080 --> 18:10.830
﻿Wh-What is it?!

18:11.040 --> 18:13.250
I'm ﻿just so extremely moved!

18:13.250 --> 18:16.260
﻿I'll help you with anything to make your dream come true!

18:16.760 --> 18:18.760
﻿You're a real samurai after all!

18:18.760 --> 18:21.010
﻿Master! That hurts!

18:21.140 --> 18:22.970
﻿We should be going now.

18:24.930 --> 18:26.640
﻿I'm glad we came here.

18:27.020 --> 18:30.770
﻿I learned a lot about Kennosuke that I never knew before.

18:31.310 --> 18:33.900
﻿A samurai from Japan, eh?

18:37.610 --> 18:39.070
﻿Nadja, what's the matter?

18:39.910 --> 18:43.070
﻿I just thought that Kennosuke is like a sunflower.

18:43.870 --> 18:46.370
﻿Facing the sun, facing his dream.

18:47.160 --> 18:49.210
﻿It gives me the feelings of not wanting to lose either.

18:49.420 --> 18:50.750
﻿Yep, he's a sunflower.

18:52.250 --> 18:54.750
﻿And, you're a wonderful sunflower, too.

18:55.960 --> 18:59.720
﻿Everyday, I'm learning so much. It's enough to make you dizzy.

19:03.350 --> 19:04.510
﻿How beautiful!

19:04.510 --> 19:07.180
﻿Did you embroider all these Mrs. Ramilez?

19:07.430 --> 19:08.180
﻿Yes.

19:08.680 --> 19:11.690
﻿The passionate patterns are native to this area.

19:11.940 --> 19:15.150
﻿Mrs. Ramilez's embroidery is the best in Spain!

19:15.150 --> 19:16.900
﻿Or rather, the best in the world!

19:18.030 --> 19:22.070
﻿Anna, however much you flatter me, I'll only take 3 orders.

19:22.780 --> 19:26.870
﻿Oh. don't say that! 5? How about just 4?

19:27.080 --> 19:30.500
﻿Won't you embroider the hats I designed?

19:30.500 --> 19:33.000
﻿I can't say no when you ask, Anna.

19:33.000 --> 19:35.290
﻿Ohhh! Thank you, Mrs. Ramilez!

19:35.670 --> 19:36.420
I know!

19:36.840 --> 19:40.720
﻿Mrs. Ramilez, would, you teach me how to do embroidery ?

19:41.090 --> 19:42.880
﻿What? All of a sudden?

19:43.090 --> 19:44.720
﻿A present for someone you like?

19:44.930 --> 19:45.890
﻿Uh...  Um...

19:45.890 --> 19:46.390
Uh... Umm...

19:46.760 --> 19:47.600
﻿It's a secret!

19:48.600 --> 19:49.680
﻿All right.

19:49.680 --> 19:51.020
﻿Thank you!

19:54.940 --> 19:56.310
﻿Must be for her "White Rose"...

19:56.860 --> 19:59.690
﻿If you want to put a woman in a good mood, a present works every time.

20:00.320 --> 20:01.150
﻿Master...

20:02.200 --> 20:04.030
﻿You want to make up with Nadja, don't you?

20:04.120 --> 20:05.120
﻿Well, yeah...

20:05.490 --> 20:08.080
﻿But, I don't have any money for presents.

20:08.240 --> 20:10.330
﻿It doesn't have to be expensive.

20:10.620 --> 20:13.790
﻿You're the one who wants to go to the moon. Use your head.

20:13.960 --> 20:14.540
﻿My head?

20:15.130 --> 20:18.500
﻿We've got junk to burn in the closet of the car.

20:18.670 --> 20:19.750
Use whatever you want.

20:19.920 --> 20:20.670
﻿Really?

20:20.920 --> 20:22.050
﻿I'll take a look!

20:28.560 --> 20:30.430
﻿I can use this!

20:51.120 --> 20:52.080
﻿Kennosuke.

20:52.500 --> 20:53.660
﻿Kennosuke!

20:54.040 --> 20:55.420
﻿Kennosuke!

20:58.040 --> 20:59.500
﻿Good morning, Kennosuke.

21:01.380 --> 21:02.840
﻿Ta-da!

21:03.220 --> 21:04.220
﻿This is...!

21:04.300 --> 21:05.010
﻿A sunflower.

21:05.930 --> 21:08.300
I'm ﻿sorry about yesterday. I said too much.

21:08.640 --> 21:10.680
﻿Please accept this with my apologies.

21:11.060 --> 21:12.350
﻿You made this for me...?

21:14.350 --> 21:17.020
﻿Thank you. I'll use it with care.

21:17.730 --> 21:20.230
﻿Now, it's my turn to give you a present.

21:20.650 --> 21:21.780
﻿Ta-da!

21:22.690 --> 21:26.150
﻿I took Abel's broken typewriter, and fixed it overnight.

21:26.280 --> 21:27.740
﻿It works beautifully now.

21:28.120 --> 21:29.370
﻿This is for me?

21:29.490 --> 21:31.200
﻿Yeah. Try it!

21:37.120 --> 21:40.170
﻿This is great!t Kennosuke, thank you!

21:40.750 --> 21:44.130
﻿Would you move over? Can I try?

21:44.130 --> 21:45.260
﻿Yes, you can!

21:45.630 --> 21:46.720
﻿Umm...

21:47.380 --> 21:48.380
﻿I know!

21:48.930 --> 21:51.010
﻿A-P-P-L-E!

21:51.010 --> 21:53.010
﻿That's right! You're doing great.

22:01.020 --> 22:04.440
﻿For me, Nadja is not a sunflower...

22:05.190 --> 22:06.570
﻿she's the sun.

